 r"I am writing to apply for the Data \& Reporting Scientist role in South West Water's Water Resources team. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. The role you describe, bringing data together from many sources, finding trends and anomalies, and turning them into reliable reporting and insight, is the kind of work I enjoy most.",

 r"What draws me to this role is that the data supports an essential public service, so accuracy really matters. Regulatory reporting and long-term planning for water resources depend on information people can trust, and I like work where checking the data properly is part of the job rather than an afterthought. I also like that the team wants to apply data science and machine learning where they help, alongside strong reporting.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I query large merchant and transaction tables in SQL and Python to find what is driving performance across the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. A large part of the work is agreeing one definition of each metric and checking the data behind it before anyone acts on it. When my supervisor asked me to set up a merchant campaign configuration by hand, I used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants. I engineered features across multiple time points, compared logistic regression with three tree-based models, checked calibration as well as accuracy, and ran sensitivity analyses before reporting anything. At DS Digital Technology I turned 4,800 free-text patient threads into structured data and scored more than 2,400 model responses against a benchmark the client adopted as its standard. At Ipsos Strategy3 I built forecasting models and turned the results into dashboards for clients.",

